Z||000000||2M4 Dale||11-18-1999||11:15 AM||||Anyone know of a good online custom wheel catalog that I could browse? I would like to look at different styles and makes before I make a decision. Wall Mart has a good line up. But I still want to shop.||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||11-18-1999||06:13 PM||||The tirerack has a great setup.  I look through their site a couple times a month.  The url is <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com/wheels/wheels.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tirerack.com/wheels/wheels.htm</A>   you may need to download a program to be able to view the cool setup.  What you do is type in your vehicle specs and it displays a picture of that vehicle and you then get to change the wheels on it.  Works real slick. They even have a picute of the Fiero, it is a red notchback coupe, but it works.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-18-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||11-19-1999||12:05 AM||||Thanks fiero56. I'll try it.||||reg||1
